 "notes": "CHECK MARKS ARE TEXT GLYPHS, NOT GRAPHICS. pdffonts on page 20 lists two embedded subset fonts AAAAAX+Wingdings2 (MacRoman, no ToUnicode) and AAAAAY+Wingdings2 (WinAnsi, ToUnicode present). pdftohtml -xml shows every check mark is the character \"R\" (U+0052) set in AAAAAY+Wingdings2 at ~22 pt; Wingdings 2 code 0x52 draws a ballot box with check (U+2611). The other font, AAAAAX+Wingdings2, carries only space characters used to pad empty cells, so empty cells contain no glyph at all. pdftotext therefore emits each checked cell as a bare \"R\" (e.g. \"Department (Adult)     R R R R R R R R R R R\"), and a naive text extraction loses the column alignment and even moves the *Helipads row of Rs above its label. Coordinates approach used for the text-layer key: pdftotext -bbox-layout -f 20 -l 20; the column x-centres come from the header abbreviations (EPS..VMC, yMin 308.92); each R glyph box (about 17.8 x 20.6 pt) is assigned to the nearest column x-centre (max offset 0.70 pt) and to the row label whose vertical centre is nearest (max offset 1.84 pt; row pitch is about 25 pt, so the assignment is not close to ambiguous). Page-20 text layer has 84 R glyphs, all black (#000000). INDEPENDENT KEYINGS: (1) text layer/bbox as above; (2) visual reading of 200-dpi renders (pdftoppm crops) cell by cell; (3) a pixel check: grid lines detected in a 200-dpi grayscale render, dark-pixel fraction inside each of the 168 cell interiors (checked cells 0.184-0.205, empty cells 0.000; no cell in between). All three agree on all 168 cells (84 checked, 84 empty); no disagreements needed reconciling. Cross-copy check: the redline copy on page 10 also has 84 R glyphs giving the identical grid. On page 10, exactly two check glyphs are blue (#0078d4) with an underline, marking tracked insertions: RSJ / STEMI Center and RSJ / Adult Trauma Center. This matches the AO 2025-005 cover memo (page 1): Regional Medical Center is designated an Adult Trauma Center and STEMI Receiving Center as of April 1, 2025. On clean page 20 those two checks are plain black. Facility full names come from Table A on the same page. EPS is not in Table A, so its name comes from the policy text. Table A prints \"STH\" for Kaiser Foundation San Jose. Asterisked rows are unregulated/supplemental per the footnote. Known currency caveat from SOURCES.md: AO 2025-006 (Sept 1 2025) and AO 2025-007 (Oct 16 2025) amend Policy 602 and are NOT captured here, so this key is exact for the April 1, 2025 document only and may not match the table currently in force."
